# AUTO-GENERATED by Claude Code
# Purpose: local OS helper CLI. `sync` applies the repo's machine setup (chezmoi source in
# .os/home/: dotfiles, packages, bashrc hook). `pwd-store` saves the 1Password master password
# in gnome-keyring (via `secret-tool`); `pwd-copy` copies it to the clipboard (wl-copy) and
# clears the clipboard after a timeout. No file is written; the keyring is per-machine.
#
# Example CLI Commands (`os` alias comes from .os/rc; new machine: run .os/install.sh first):
#   1. Pull + preview + apply setup:         os sync
#   2. Preview only:                         os sync --dry-run --no-pull
#   3. Store (hidden prompt, asked twice):   os pwd-store
#   4. Copy to clipboard (clears after 5s):  os pwd-copy
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


